The `.siliguri-stroke` CSS class was inverted — it rendered the "Siliguri" text with a transparent fill and a green stroke, instead of the intended green fill with a white outline.

## Changes

- **`app/globals.css`**: Corrected `.siliguri-stroke` rule:
  - `color` → `var(--brand-green)` (was `transparent`)
  - `-webkit-text-stroke` → `1px white` (was `1px var(--brand-green)`)
  - Added `text-shadow: 0 0 1px white` for legibility on dark backgrounds

```css
/* Before */
.siliguri-stroke {
  -webkit-text-stroke: 1px var(--brand-green);
  color: transparent;
}

/* After */
.siliguri-stroke {
  color: var(--brand-green);
  -webkit-text-stroke: 1px white;
  text-shadow: 0 0 1px white;
}
```

`Hero.tsx` already had the correct markup (`<span className="text-brand-green siliguri-stroke">`); only the CSS needed fixing.

